BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2e356e01-ed4b-406c-8cf5-d17e357fe1b9@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260708T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260708T181500
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=WE
SUMMARY:Wednesday Batch Cook — Vegetable Khichdi (Week 1)
DESCRIPTION:RECIPE — Vegetable Khichdi: 1 cup rice + 1/2 cup moong dal\, 
 rinsed together. 3 cups mixed chopped vegetables (carrot\, beans\, peas\, 
 potato). 4.5 cups water\, 1/2 tsp turmeric\, 1 tsp cumin seeds\, 1 tbsp gh
 ee\, salt to taste.\nMETHOD (Instant Pot): saute cumin in ghee 30 sec -> a
 dd rice\, dal\, vegetables\, turmeric\, salt\, water -> Manual/Pressure Co
 ok 8 min -> natural release 10 min.\nAHANA: set aside and mash her portion
  before adding final salt/chili if any is added at serving.\nThis doubles 
 as tonight's dinner — no separate cooking needed at 6:00.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0151f09e-b150-4831-9e54-03f3dc43e279@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260715T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260715T181500
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=WE
SUMMARY:Wednesday Batch Cook — Vegetable Pulao (Week 2)
DESCRIPTION:RECIPE — Vegetable Pulao: 2 cups basmati rice\, rinsed. 2 cup
 s mixed vegetables (peas\, carrot\, beans). 1 sliced onion\, 1 tbsp ginger
 -garlic paste. Whole spices: 1 bay leaf\, 2 cloves\, 1 small cinnamon stic
 k\, 2 cardamom pods. 2 tbsp ghee\, 3.5 cups water\, salt.\nMETHOD (Instant
  Pot): saute whole spices + onion in ghee 3 min -> add ginger-garlic\, veg
 etables\, rice\, water\, salt -> Manual/Pressure Cook 6 min -> natural rel
 ease 10 min.\nAHANA: set aside and mash her portion before serving with an
 y extra chili.\nDoubles as tonight's dinner.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:431c4900-a8d1-4edc-a3c0-e9905016c91c@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260722T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260722T181500
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=WE
SUMMARY:Wednesday Batch Cook — Dal Khichdi + Roasted Veg (Week 3)
DESCRIPTION:RECIPE — Dal Khichdi: 1/3 cup toor dal + 1/3 cup moong dal + 
 1 cup rice\, rinsed together. 4 cups water\, 1/2 tsp turmeric\, salt.\nMET
 HOD (Instant Pot): combine all -> Manual/Pressure Cook 8 min -> natural re
 lease.\nRoasted veg (air fryer\, cook alongside): 3 cups mixed vegetables 
 (cauliflower\, carrot\, sweet potato) tossed in 1 tbsp oil\, salt\, 1/2 ts
 p cumin powder -> 400F\, 15 min\, shake at 8 min.\nAHANA: her portion asid
 e before any final chili goes on the khichdi.\nDoubles as tonight's dinner
 .
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:16354b6c-96ce-4a12-8750-be9722c1b694@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260729T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260729T181500
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=WE
SUMMARY:Wednesday Batch Cook — Lemon Rice + Air-Fryer Tofu (Week 4)
DESCRIPTION:RECIPE — Lemon Rice: 3 cups cooked rice (Sunday's batch\, or 
 fresh). Temper 2 tbsp oil\, 1 tsp mustard seeds\, 1 tbsp chana dal\, 1 tbs
 p peanuts\, curry leaves\, 2 dried red chilies\, pinch turmeric -> mix int
 o rice with juice of 1.5 lemons\, salt.\nRECIPE — Tofu (air fryer\, cook
  alongside): 14 oz tofu cubes tossed in 2 tbsp yogurt + 1 tbsp ginger-garl
 ic paste + 1 tsp chili powder + 1/2 tsp turmeric + 1 tsp garam masala + 3/
 4 tsp salt + 1 tbsp oil -> 400F\, 12 min\, shake at 6 min.\nAHANA: plain r
 ice portion aside before the lemon/chili tempering goes in.\nDoubles as to
 night's dinner.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ae56874a-a5eb-43fb-8492-ad2750b3f231@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260706T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260706T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Tadka Dal + Aloo Gobi + Rice (
 Week 1)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: reheat Sunday's batch dal (1 cup toor dal base)
  with a fresh tempering — 1 tbsp ghee\, 1 tsp cumin seeds\, 2 crushed ga
 rlic cloves\, 1 dried red chili\, pinch hing\; pour over dal\, simmer 3 mi
 n.\nAloo gobi: 2 cups cauliflower florets + 2 medium potatoes\, cubed. Hea
 t 2 tbsp oil + 1 tsp cumin seeds\, add potato/cauliflower\, 1/2 tsp turmer
 ic\, 1 tsp coriander powder\, 1/2 tsp red chili powder\, salt. Cover\, coo
 k 12-15 min\, stir occasionally\, finish with cilantro.\nServe over Sunday
 's batch rice. Ahana: her portion aside before final chili.\nProtected\, w
 ork paused — dinner (~6:30) + floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:07717c17-50c9-4e04-9d9b-5d2bd3b90d77@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260713T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260713T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Chana Dal + Bhindi Fry + Rice 
 (Week 2)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: Chana dal — 1 cup chana dal\, Instant Pot Man
 ual 12 min + natural release\, with 3 cups water\, 1/2 tsp turmeric\, salt
 . Temper: 1 tbsp oil\, 1 tsp cumin\, 1 chopped onion\, 1 tomato\, 1/2 tsp 
 red chili powder — cook till soft\, mix in\, simmer 5 min.\nBhindi fry: 
 3 cups sliced okra\, saute uncovered in 2 tbsp oil\, medium-high\, 12-15 m
 in\, with 1/2 tsp turmeric\, 1 tsp coriander powder\, salt\, until crisp-e
 dged (uncovered keeps it from getting slimy).\nServe with rice. Ahana: her
  portion aside before final chili.\nProtected\, work paused — dinner (~6
 :30) + floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:42657bee-0bac-4465-a8b5-d84e09483da4@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260720T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260720T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Moong Dal + Baingan Bharta + R
 oti (Week 3)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: Moong dal — 1 cup split moong dal\, Instant P
 ot Manual 6 min + quick release\, 1/2 tsp turmeric\, salt\, 3 cups water. 
 Temper: 1 tbsp ghee\, 1 tsp cumin\, pinch hing\, 1 chopped tomato — mix 
 in.\nBaingan bharta: roast 1 large eggplant whole (air fryer 400F\, 25 min
 ) until soft\, peel\, mash. Saute 1 chopped onion\, 2 cloves garlic\, 1 to
 mato in 2 tbsp oil\, add mashed eggplant\, 1/2 tsp turmeric\, 1/2 tsp red 
 chili powder\, salt\, cook 8 min.\nServe with fresh roti. Ahana: her porti
 on aside before final chili.\nProtected\, work paused — dinner (~6:30) +
  floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f178eef4-7515-4dd0-ad1c-e70b9d5bbbc5@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260727T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260727T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Rajma + Jeera Rice (Week 4)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: Rajma — 1 cup rajma (soaked overnight\, or ca
 nned & drained)\, Instant Pot Manual 20 min soaked / 8 min canned + natura
 l release\, with 1 chopped onion\, 1 tomato\, 1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste\,
  1 tsp rajma masala or garam masala\, salt\, 2.5 cups water.\nJeera rice: 
 2 cups basmati rice — saute 1 tbsp ghee + 1 tsp cumin seeds first\, then
  cook rice as usual (rice cooker) with the cumin-ghee mixed in.\nAhana: he
 r portion aside before final chili.\nProtected\, work paused — dinner (~
 6:30) + floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9c21a8ce-96d2-4561-b198-f944542e0063@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260707T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260707T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TU
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Sambar + Rice + Beans Poriyal 
 (Week 1)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: Sambar — reheat 1.5 cups leftover dal base\, 
 add 1 cup mixed vegetables (drumstick\, carrot\, pumpkin — whatever's on
  hand)\, 2 tbsp sambar powder\, 1 tbsp tamarind paste\, salt. Simmer 10 mi
 n. Temper: 1 tbsp oil\, 1/2 tsp mustard seeds\, curry leaves\, 2 dried red
  chilies — pour over.\nBeans poriyal: 2 cups chopped green beans\, saute
 /steam 8 min with 1 tbsp oil\, 1/2 tsp mustard seeds\, curry leaves\, 2 tb
 sp grated coconut\, salt.\nServe with rice. Ahana: her portion aside befor
 e final tempering.\nProtected\, work paused — dinner (~6:30) + floor pla
 y or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0b3ce5a4-7308-479c-a02e-c0bf24970a5e@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260714T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260714T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TU
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Rasam + Rice + Cabbage Poriyal
  (Week 2)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: Rasam — 2 tbsp cooked toor dal mashed + 2 cup
 s water\, 1 tbsp rasam powder\, 1 tbsp tamarind paste\, 1 chopped tomato\,
  salt. Simmer 10 min. Temper: 1 tsp mustard seeds\, curry leaves\, pinch h
 ing in 1 tbsp ghee — pour over\, finish with cilantro.\nCabbage poriyal:
  3 cups shredded cabbage\, saute 8 min with 1 tbsp oil\, 1/2 tsp mustard s
 eeds\, 2 tbsp grated coconut\, salt.\nServe with rice. Ahana: her portion 
 aside before final tempering.\nProtected\, work paused — dinner (~6:30) 
 + floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a9c99caf-7dc2-4214-b0fc-1d64acfd63a8@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260721T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260721T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TU
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Vegetable Kurma + Idli (Week 3
 )
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: Kurma — saute 1 chopped onion\, 1 tbsp ginger
 -garlic paste in 2 tbsp oil\, add 2 cups mixed vegetables (carrot\, beans\
 , potato\, peas)\, 1/2 cup coconut-cashew paste (blend 3 tbsp grated cocon
 ut + 5 cashews + water)\, 1 tsp garam masala\, salt\, 1 cup water — simm
 er covered 12 min.\nServe with steamed idli (store-bought batter is fine).
 \nAhana: her portion aside before final spice.\nProtected\, work paused 
 — dinner (~6:30) + floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5d2d4896-0f08-4c23-93e7-d521eff0607d@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260728T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260728T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TU
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Curd Rice + Vathal Kuzhambu (W
 eek 4)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: Curd rice — mix 2 cups cooked rice (mashed sl
 ightly) with 1.5 cups yogurt\, 1/2 cup milk\, salt. Temper 1 tsp mustard s
 eeds\, curry leaves\, 1 dried red chili in 1 tbsp oil — mix in.\nVathal 
 kuzhambu — 2 tbsp tamarind paste + 1.5 cups water\, 2 tbsp sambar powder
 \, salt\, simmer 10 min\, same temper as sambar. (Short on time: leftover 
 sambar works as a substitute.)\nAhana: plain curd rice\, no tempering\, se
 t aside first.\nProtected\, work paused — dinner (~6:30) + floor play or
  books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7884a09a-92a8-4e0f-a96f-f38a60f88fb6@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260708T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260708T193000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=WE
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — dinner already cooking
DESCRIPTION:Tonight's dinner and its exact recipe are in the 5:45-6:15 PM '
 Wednesday Batch Cook' event — nothing new to decide here. Just serve\, e
 at (~6:30)\, then floor play or books\, her choice. No phones.\n\nIf it's 
 your week to own the Wednesday refresh (alternates — check the reset)\, 
 you're the one cooking\; otherwise Prakash has it if he's less deep in a w
 ork block tonight.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:db46d6b4-4ea2-47ee-a581-497c1ac0e0a7@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260709T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260709T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TH
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Dal Paratha\, ~10 min (Week 1)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT (leftover remix): mix 1 cup leftover thick dal w
 ith 1.5 cups whole wheat flour\, 1/2 tsp ajwain\, salt\, a splash of water
  — knead into a soft dough. Roll into 6 parathas\, cook on a hot tawa wi
 th 1/2 tsp ghee each side until golden spots appear. Serve with yogurt/pic
 kle.\nAhana: a plain paratha\, no pickle\, torn into small pieces.\nProtec
 ted\, work paused — dinner (~6:30) + floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d5601cd4-bec9-4645-a5d4-a4004bd8af90@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260716T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TH
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Fried Rice\, ~10 min (Week 2)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT (leftover remix): 3 cups leftover rice\, 1 cup d
 iced mixed vegetables (frozen is fine) — saute vegetables in 2 tbsp oil 
 4 min\, push aside\, scramble in 2 eggs or extra tofu cubes\, mix in rice\
 , 2 tbsp soy sauce\, 1/2 tsp black pepper\, toss 3-4 min on high heat.\nAh
 ana: a plain portion set aside before the soy sauce goes in.\nProtected\, 
 work paused — dinner (~6:30) + floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a2a82344-b77f-438e-9a46-621922a34107@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260723T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260723T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TH
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Dal Soup + Toast\, ~10 min (We
 ek 3)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT (leftover remix): blend or mash 1.5 cups leftove
 r dal with 1 cup vegetable broth or water to soup consistency\, reheat wit
 h a squeeze of lemon and black pepper. Toast 4 slices bread with butter. D
 one in 5 minutes.\nAhana: her portion without the lemon/pepper\, lukewarm.
 \nProtected\, work paused — dinner (~6:30) + floor play or books\, her c
 hoice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cc899342-996d-4d08-bbcb-31c1d8740cdc@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260730T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260730T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=TH
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Rajma Wrap\, ~10 min (Week 4)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT (leftover remix): warm 4 tortillas or rotis. Fil
 l with leftover rajma (mash slightly so it doesn't spill)\, chopped onion\
 , a spoon of yogurt or chutney\, shredded lettuce. Roll and serve — rehe
 ating only\, no real cooking.\nAhana: rajma and rice separately rather tha
 n wrapped\, easier for her to eat.\nProtected\, work paused — dinner (~6
 :30) + floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:61702d12-32b0-4636-95c0-9d8d1f95ff4c@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260710T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260710T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=FR
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Dosa/Uttapam\, batter (Week 1)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: heat a tawa\, pour a ladle of batter — spread
  thin for dosa\, or leave thick with chopped onion/tomato pressed in for u
 ttapam. Cook 2-3 min per side with a little oil. Serve with sambar (Tuesda
 y's leftovers\, if any) and coconut chutney (store-bought is fine).\nAhana
 : a soft\, plain uttapam piece\, torn small.\nProtected\, work paused — 
 dinner (~6:30) + floor play or books\, her choice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dcfa432d-9fc7-4c45-9c42-b6e5be880988@family-os
DTSTAMP:20260707T120000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260717T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260717T193000
RRULE:INTERVAL=4;FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=FR
SUMMARY:Family block\, no phones — Dinner: Pasta Night (Week 2)
DESCRIPTION:DINNER TONIGHT: boil 300g pasta per package instructions. Sauce
 : saute 1 chopped onion + 3 cloves garlic in 2 tbsp olive oil\, add 1 cup 
 jarred marinara + 1 cup chopped vegetables (zucchini\, bell pepper\, spina
 ch)\, simmer 8 min\, salt + chili flakes to taste. Toss with pasta\, top w
